1. Definitions
(a) "Software" means ClaudeOffice (a Claude Code session dashboard for Windows; the app is named "Claude 사무실"), its installer, portable executable, automatic update feature, source code, pixel-art graphics (characters, buildings, furniture, backgrounds), icons, documentation, introduction page, and every file contained in this repository.
(b) "Licensor" means BlackBuddle (GitHub account), named in the copyright notice above.
(c) "Personal User" means an individual (natural person) who uses the Software for himself or herself, without any commercial purpose.
(d) "Optional Component" means a component made by someone other than the Licensor that the user chooses to download and use through a feature of the Software (for example Ollama or the Qwen3 model). Optional Components are not included in the Software and are not part of it.
(e) "Official Distribution" means the Releases of this repository (https://github.com/BlackBuddle/ClaudeOffice-releases); the introduction page is https://blackbuddle.github.io/ClaudeOffice-releases/.

2. Grant
The Licensor grants each Personal User, as long as this license is followed, the right to install and run the Software on his or her own computer and to use it free of charge for personal purposes. This right is non-exclusive, non-transferable, cannot be sublicensed, and may end or be withdrawn under Section 8.

3. What is not allowed
Without the Licensor's prior written permission, you may not:
(a) use the Software for the business or commercial activities of a company, school, organization or institution (use by an individual on his or her own computer as a hobby is not restricted);
(b) sell, rent, lease, host, offer the Software as a service, or include it in another product;
(c) copy, distribute, publish or transmit the Software or any part of it, including modified versions (copying it to install it on your own computer is allowed);
(d) modify the Software or create derivative works (except as permitted by law, and except changing the settings the Software provides);
(e) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software to obtain source code (except as permitted by law);
(f) remove or change the copyright notices, trademark notices, or the notices of this license and the disclaimer;
(g) use the Software to harm others or to break the law (including viewing or collecting another person's Claude Code sessions or conversation records without that person's consent);
(h) Viewing or forking a public repository within GitHub is permitted only to the extent allowed by GitHub's Terms of Service and does not grant any right not granted by this license.

4. Your data and settings
Your Claude Code sessions, conversations, command texts and settings, and what the Software shows or summarizes from them, belong to you; the Licensor claims no rights in them. Optional Components and third-party services are subject to their providers' own terms, and this license does not apply to them.

5. Third-party components and trademarks
(a) The Software contains open-source components such as Electron, Chromium, Node.js and Python. Each component remains under its own license; this license does not change them. The included components and their licenses are listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
(b) Optional Components (such as Ollama and the Qwen3 model) are governed by their own licenses and their providers' terms when you download them.
(c) "Claude", "Anthropic" and related names and logos are trademarks of Anthropic PBC. This is a personal project and is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or approved by Anthropic.

6. Ownership
The copyright and all other rights in the Software belong to the Licensor. This license grants only a right of use and does not transfer ownership. All rights not expressly granted are reserved by the Licensor.

7. No warranty and disclaimer
The Software is provided free of charge "AS IS". Warranties and liability are governed by the accompanying disclaimer (DISCLAIMER.md), which is part of this license.

8. Term and termination
This license begins when you receive the Software. If you breach this license it ends automatically without notice, and you must stop using the Software and delete all copies. The Licensor may withdraw permission for future use at any time. The Software is free, so no refund applies.

9. Other uses
Uses not allowed by Section 3 (business or commercial use, redistribution, etc.) require the Licensor's written permission. Please ask through the Issues of the Official Distribution repository (https://github.com/BlackBuddle/ClaudeOffice-releases/issues). Do not post sensitive information in public.

10. Governing law and jurisdiction
This license is interpreted under the laws of the Republic of Korea, and jurisdiction over disputes follows the Korean Civil Procedure Act.

11. Severability and changes
If any part of this license is invalid or unenforceable, the rest remains in force. The Licensor may change this license; a new version applies from the time it is posted to the Official Distribution to Software received or updated after that time. Updating the Software through the automatic update feature counts as an update.
